# Return the Favor with both modes, its copy mode's target gone (CR 608.2b): Bot2 casts two Lightning Bolts at Bot1. Bot1
# answers with Return the Favor for {R}{R}{1}{1} (Black Lotus and Mox Ruby), copying the first Bolt and changing the target
# of the second, then, holding priority, Counterspells the first Bolt (Island and Mox Sapphire). The change mode's target
# is still legal, so Return the Favor resolves: the copy mode, its target illegal, copies nothing (a spell that has left
# the stack would otherwise be copied as it last was), and the second Bolt is turned to Bot2, the only other legal target.
# Bot2 takes 3; Bot1 none.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Return the Favor
Counterspell
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Return the Favor.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Copy target; Change the target)
Bot1.Target(Stack.Lightning Bolt#2)
Bot1.Target(Stack.Lightning Bolt#1)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Lightning Bolt#2)
? Stack.Count = 4
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Return the Favor; Counterspell; Black Lotus
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt
Stack.Count = 0
